# MCP Browser Client Project Structure

MCP Browser Client is a system for testing MCP (Model Context Protocol) client libraries in the browser and building applications on them, centered on the agent loop: a model choosing tools and using them. Everything runs in a web page and a service worker shared by every tab, delivered as a static site, with nothing to install or configure locally.

## Core Components

### MCP client libraries (pluggable)
- Registry and loaders: [public/mcp-clients.js](mdc:public/mcp-clients.js) (`MCP_CLIENTS`, `DEFAULT_CLIENT`, `loadMcpClient`)
- The worker's active library: [public/client-runtime.js](mdc:public/client-runtime.js) (`setClient`, `ensureClient`, ...); the choice persists in Cache Storage
- TypeScript SDK library (`sdk`, default): [sdk-client/index.js](mdc:sdk-client/index.js), an adapter over `@modelcontextprotocol/client`
- Rust/WASM library (`wasm`): [src/lib.rs](mdc:src/lib.rs) exports; protocol in `src/mcp/`, sign-in in `src/oauth/`
- Every library implements the same interface (JSON strings in and out, JSON `McpError` rejections), documented in [DEVELOPMENT.md](mdc:DEVELOPMENT.md)

### Service Worker
- Implementation: [public/sw.js](mdc:public/sw.js)
  - Routes page messages to the active library (`mcpClient`); never builds JSON-RPC itself
  - Owns sign-in storage (`authStore.js`), run history (`workbench/store.js`) and conversations (`chatStorage.js`)
  - Runs the Chat app's agent loop (`handleToolCall`, `modelArguments`, `extractJsonRpcCalls`, `runReplyToolCall`), with its built-in instructions in [public/chat-instructions.js](mdc:public/chat-instructions.js)

### Web Interface
- Page: [public/index.html](mdc:public/index.html)
 - The top bar (Runtime menu with the library picker `#clientSelect`), the layout, the Apps page (the Chat app and the app builder) and the Guide
 - `AppShell`, the controller: talks to the service worker, owns servers, sign-in, tool calls, resource reads and prompt gets, and emits events instead of drawing UI
- Workbench: [public/workbench/](mdc:public/workbench/index.js)
  - One custom element per part of the screen in `components/` (rail, server bar, tools with the Resources and Prompts tabs, request, resource, prompt, response, contents, splitter, dock, sheet, palette)
  - Shared state in `workbench.js`; the layout is grid areas in `workbench.css`, sized by the splitters' CSS variables
  - Resource templates' URIs in `uri-template.js` (RFC 6570); Pre-fill's test data in `prefill.js`
- App builder: [public/apps/](mdc:public/apps/index.js)
 - An app is a screen (components, or HTML from a tool call) and a flow (rules: when, call, then); the state is `apps.js`, the components are in `components/` (rail, header, Screen, Flow, Try it)
 - `runner.js` runs an app: its screen in a sandboxed frame (`frameRuntime`, `frameDocument`), its flow in the page, each call through `AppShell.runTool` with source `app`
 - `flow.js` (templates, arguments, problems, sentences) and `screen.js` are pure; `dml.js` reads and writes the DML an app downloads as, `zip.js` the zip, `store.js` keeps apps in IndexedDB `mcp_apps`

## Build System
- `npm run build` builds every library: `npm run build:sdk` ([sdk-client/build.mjs](mdc:sdk-client/build.mjs), esbuild) and `npm run build:wasm` ([wasm-build.sh](mdc:wasm-build.sh), [Cargo.toml](mdc:Cargo.toml))
- Each build writes a hash file (`public/build.js`, `public/build-sdk.js`) that `mcp-clients.js` imports, so a rebuild is a worker update

## Testing and measuring
- `npm run test:browser` (the default library; `--client=sdk|wasm`, `--reference`), `npm run test:browser:wasm`, `npm run test:rust`
- `npm run test:unit` ([tests/prefill.test.mjs](mdc:tests/prefill.test.mjs), [tests/uri-template.test.mjs](mdc:tests/uri-template.test.mjs), [tests/apps.test.mjs](mdc:tests/apps.test.mjs)): Pre-fill's test data from [public/workbench/prefill.js](mdc:public/workbench/prefill.js), validated with Ajv, resource template URIs against RFC 6570's examples, and the app builder's DML, zips and flow
- `npm run bench` ([tests/bench.mjs](mdc:tests/bench.mjs), [public/bench/](mdc:public/bench/index.html)): tool-call throughput per library

## Naming
- Say "MCP client library" (or "library") for the pluggable protocol implementation, and use `client` in code: `set_client`, `client_loaded`, `client_status`, `?client=`, `--client=`
- The Chat app's agent loop says conversation (`conversationId`), model (`set_chat_model`, `messageField`, `conversationField`), context (`set_chat_context`) and instructions (`public/chat-instructions.js`). Its first version's names (engram, CBus tap, imprints, bootrom) only survive in the code that moves old stored data over
- The app builder says app, screen, component, element (anything with an id), flow, rule (`when`, `call`, `then`), route (one `then`) and DML (the markup an app downloads as, `app.dml`)
